new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3d7a5d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/windows.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Experimental Windows / WHPX host
+
+This local port targets native x86-64 Windows with the Vulkan feature and QEMU WHPX. It does not require GPU partitioning. The guest uses Apple's existing AppleParavirtGPU driver; Metal commands are translated through metal2vulkan-runtime to the host Vulkan driver.
+
+Build with the GNU Rust toolchain and MSYS2 UCRT64 development tools:
+
+```sh
+cargo build -p reims-vgpu-c --release --no-default-features --features vulkan
+```
+
+The workspace currently patches metal2vulkan and its runtime to the sibling `../metal2vulkan-windows` checkout. This is a development dependency, not a published package. The runtime needs the Windows rotation, page-size, sharing and exit-guard changes in that checkout. Firmware uses llvm-objcopy on Windows. QEMU is a separate local experimental checkout with WHPX fixes and section-backed RAM.
+
+## Memory and API
+
+Windows RAM is backed by pagefile sections. `RvgDeviceConfig.memory_sections` is an additive, size-checked extension: each range supplies a borrowed native section handle and its byte offset. Creation duplicates handles and validates the range. These are not Unix file descriptors. The QEMU host must allocate RAM from shared sections and provide their handles; callback-only RAM cannot supply aliasable guest memory.
+
+VirtualAlloc2 placeholders and MapViewOfFile3 provide fixed aliases, partial replacement and independent backing lifetimes. GPU virtual-address reservations use uncommitted placeholders rather than pagefile-backed allocations. Host memory imported into Vulkan retains its writable alias until the runtime releases it. Vulkan external-host-memory support and compatible alignment are required. DMA-BUF remains Unix-only.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+A local Windows 11 / RTX 4070 SUPER run booted an independent Sonoma 14.8.9 disk copy using WHPX. The guest loaded AppleParavirtGPUControl, reported Metal 2, and rendered the 1920x1080 desktop. Host logs showed translated render and compute work. Eight window drag round trips updated the display without stopping the guest. A QMP hardware reset recovered the Metal device; this is not a guest-initiated clean reboot test.
+
+Seven actual-source memory tests cover alias lifetime, partial replacement, refusal rollback, maximum protections, a 1 TiB sparse reservation and surface ownership. The runtime host-memory selection passed 11 tests, and a native Vulkan import/fill/readback test passed.
+
+The validated presentation path is headless QMP capture (`REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW=0`). Native SDL presentation, video decode, performance, long-duration stability, Linux/macOS regression checks and the full behavior-lock suite remain unverified. This is a local experiment, not an upstream-ready or production-supported port.
